        {"w": "カカオ", "r": "kakao", "m": "cacao"},
        {"w": "キウイ", "r": "kiui", "m": "kiwi"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ja0-9",
      "title": "Katakana words",
      "learn": [
        {"h": "English in disguise", "p": "Most katakana words are borrowed from English (or other languages) and reshaped into Japanese sounds. Every consonant gets a vowel after it, so “television” became <b>テレビ</b> (terebi) and “taxi” became <b>タクシー</b> (takushī). Say them out loud and you can often guess the meaning!", "ex": ["ja-terebi", "ja-takushii"]}
      ],
      "items": [
        {"id": "ja-koohii", "w": "コーヒー", "r": "kōhī", "m": "coffee", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "ja-terebi", "w": "テレビ", "r": "terebi", "m": "TV", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "ja-kamera", "w": "カメラ", "r": "kamera", "m": "camera", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "ja-pan", "w": "パン", "r": "pan", "m": "bread", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "ja-keeki", "w": "ケーキ", "r": "kēki", "m": "cake", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "ja-aisu", "w": "アイス", "r": "aisu", "m": "ice cream", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "ja-takushii", "w": "タクシー", "r": "takushī", "m": "taxi", "kind": "word"}
      ],
      "build": [
        {"w": "ホテル", "r": "hoteru", "m": "hotel"},
        {"w": "バス", "r": "basu", "m": "bus"},
        {"w": "トマト", "r": "tomato", "m": "tomato"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ja0-10",
      "title": "First words",
      "learn": [
        {"h": "High and low pitch", "p": "Instead of English-style stress, Japanese words have a <b>pitch melody</b> of high and low beats. はし can mean “chopsticks” or “bridge” depending on the melody. For now, just copy the melody you hear."},
        {"h": "Kanji preview", "p": "Many words are written with kanji: <b>山</b> (やま yama, mountain), <b>人</b> (ひと hito, person). The same characters exist in Chinese with the same meanings, a head start for both languages!", "ex": ["ja-yama", "ja-hito"]}
      ],
      "items": [
        {"id": "ja-konnichiwa", "w": "こんにちは", "r": "konnichiwa", "say": "こんにちわ", "m": "hello", "kind": "word", "hint": "the final は is read “wa”"},
